# MM PortLens language file – English (reference / template)
#
# How to add a new language (no recompiling needed):
#   1. Copy this file and name it by the language code, e.g. "fr.lang", "pl.lang", "pt-BR.lang".
#   2. Translate the text after "=" on every line. Keep the key before "=" unchanged.
#   3. Keep placeholders in curly braces, e.g. {count}, {error}, unchanged (their order may change).
#   4. Put the file into one of these folders:
#        - "lang" next to mmportlens.exe
#        - %APPDATA%\MMPortLens\lang   (Linux: ~/.config/MMPortLens/lang)
#   5. Restart the program and pick the language in View → Language.
#
# Format: one "key = value" per line, lines starting with # are comments,
# "\n" in a value is a line break. Missing keys fall back to English.

